    "narrative": "The Austin Waves look to capitalize on a favorable schedule today, headlined by **Gunnar Henderson**, whose 83.29 score makes him our clear offensive anchor. Facing a weak arm in Johnson (xERA 4.96) in a hitter-friendly environment, **Gunnar Henderson** benefits from a massive 35% cumulative boost from park and pitcher skill factors. **Luis Robert Jr.** and **Drake Baldwin** also project as strong starts; **Luis Robert Jr.** carries significant upside against a lefty due to his dynamic platoon advantage, while **Drake Baldwin** earns a spot at the top of the lineup, leveraging the high-volume opportunities inherent in the leadoff role to pad our counting stats.\n\nThe most difficult decision on today\u2019s card was leaving **Luis Lara** on the bench. With a score of 37.66, he fell just shy of our 40.0 efficiency floor; while his switch-hitting versatility is valuable, the combination of an elite arm in Ashcraft (xERA 3.35) and a slight park penalty pushed him below our threshold. Meanwhile, we continue to monitor our IL situations, as **Jordan Westburg** remains unavailable, and both **Kyle Tucker** and **Andy Pages** are sidelined by team off-days. We are proceeding with caution regarding **Nasim Nunez**; despite his elite speed, his score of 40.23 is suppressed by a difficult matchup against S\u00e1nchez (xERA 2.86) and a high opponent catcher hold rate, limiting his stolen base ceiling today. \n\nWe will continue to manage the remaining depth\u2014including **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**, **Jacob Wilson**, **Jorge Polanco**, **Heliot Ramos**, **Josh Jung**, **Coby Mayo**, **Curtis Mead**, **Sam Antonacci**, and **Liam Hicks**\u2014to ensure we maximize our daily caps. **Wade Meckler** earns the nod in the UTIL spot today, riding a surge of momentum from strong park and SP skill factors that elevate his projection to 59.97, just narrowly missing our \"Strong\" tier but providing enough reliability to justify the start over available depth.",
